    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0776" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/10–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in Saudi
                        Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-03T19:00:00-04:00">November 3, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>234. You are authorized to approach the Saudi Government requesting establishment
                    of direct radiotelegraph service between the United States and Saudi Arabia,
                    with notification to Cable and Wireless before December 1. Details of new
                    station and its operation to be settled later if necessary as suggested in your
                    317 October 22 and 322 October 28.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d835-f1"/> For your
                    information it is understood that it would take at least 5 months for station to
                    be shipped from this country and placed in operation in Saudi Arabia by which
                    time war in Europe might well be over. You are further advised that question of
                    direct circuit and British objection thereto is being taken up with London in
                    strongest possible terms. You will be kept advised of developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
